00:01:04.280 --> 00:01:07.670
Hey, Bert, come on out and meet all these nice people, please.

00:01:08.630 --> 00:01:09.630
Oh, all right.

00:01:09.910 --> 00:01:11.070
We really can't blame you.

00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:14.420
You see, Bert is a very, very careful fellow.

00:01:15.140 --> 00:01:18.110
As danger, this is the way he keeps from being hurt.

00:01:19.070 --> 00:01:21.510
Sometimes it even saves his life.

00:01:22.780 --> 00:01:27.700
That's why these children are practicing to duck and cover just as you do in your school.

00:01:28.740 --> 00:01:29.980
We all know the atomic...

00:01:30.030 --> 00:01:35.790
bomb is very dangerous. Since it may be used against us, we must get ready for it, just as we

00:01:35.790 --> 00:01:41.940
are ready for many other dangers that are around us all the time. Fire is a danger. It can burn

00:01:41.940 --> 00:01:48.680
whole buildings if someone is careless. But we are ready for fire. We have a fine fire department

00:01:48.680 --> 00:01:55.410
to put out the fire. And you have fire drills in your school so you know what to do. Automobiles

00:01:55.410 --> 00:01:59.840
can be dangerous too. They sometimes cause bad accidents. But we are ready.

00:02:00.220 --> 00:02:03.840
We have safety rules that car drivers and people who are walking must obey.

00:02:04.790 --> 00:02:09.020
Now, we must be ready for a new danger, the atomic bomb.

00:02:10.270 --> 00:02:13.500
First, you'll have to know what happens when an atomic bomb explodes.

00:02:14.280 --> 00:02:15.560
You'll know when it comes.

00:02:15.980 --> 00:02:18.290
We hope it never comes, but we must get ready.

00:02:18.980 --> 00:02:20.020
It looks something like this.

00:02:20.780 --> 00:02:24.460
There is a bright flash, brighter than the sun, brighter than anything you've ever seen.

00:02:25.520 --> 00:02:29.770
If you were not ready and did not know what to do, it could hurt you.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:36.590
different ways. It could knock you down hard or throw you against a tree or a wall. It is such a

00:02:36.590 --> 00:02:42.640
big explosion, it can smash in buildings and knock sign boards over and break windows all over town.

00:02:43.090 --> 00:02:50.720
But if you duck and cover like Bert, you will be much safer. You know how bad sunburn can feel.

00:02:51.320 --> 00:02:55.080
The atomic bomb flash could burn you worse than a terrible sunburn,

00:02:55.650 --> 00:02:59.800
especially where you're not covered. Now, you and I don't have shells.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:06.670
crawl into like Bert the turtle, so we have to cover up in our own way. First, you duck, and then

00:03:06.670 --> 00:03:14.420
you cover, and very tightly, you cover the back of your neck, your face. Duck and cover underneath a

00:03:14.420 --> 00:03:20.700
table, or desk, or anything else close by. In Betty's school, they are talking about the atomic

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:27.880
bomb too. Betty is asking her teacher, how can we tell when the atomic bomb may explode? And her

00:03:27.880 --> 00:03:29.960
The teacher is explaining that there are two kinds of...

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:36.140
attack, with warning and without any warning. We think that most of the time we will be warned

00:03:36.140 --> 00:03:42.130
before the bomb explodes, so there will be time for us to get into our homes, schools, or some

00:03:42.130 --> 00:03:48.380
other safe place. Our civil defense workers and our men in uniform will do everything they can

00:03:48.380 --> 00:03:55.460
to warn us before enemy planes can bring a bomb near us. You may be in your schoolyard playing

00:03:55.460 --> 00:03:56.540
when the signal comes.

00:04:00.160 --> 00:04:05.400
That signal means to stop whatever you are doing and get to the nearest safe place fast.

00:04:06.370 --> 00:04:12.240
Always remember, a flash of an atomic bomb can come at any time, no matter where you may be.

00:04:13.460 --> 00:04:16.000
You might be out playing at home when the warning comes.

00:04:18.690 --> 00:04:24.280
Then be sure to get into the house fast, where your parents have fixed a safe place for you to go.

00:04:25.570 --> 00:04:29.920
If you are not close to home when you hear the warning, go to the nearest safe cover.

00:04:30.890 --> 00:04:37.270
know where you are to go or ask an older person to help you you know the places marked with the s

00:04:37.270 --> 00:04:44.160
sign there are safe places to go when you hear the alarm if there is a warning you will hear it

00:04:44.160 --> 00:04:52.180
before the bomb explodes but sometimes and this is very very important sometimes the bomb might

00:04:52.180 --> 00:04:58.930
explode without any warning then the first thing we would know about it would be the flash and that

00:04:58.930 --> 00:04:59.890
means duck and

00:05:00.030 --> 00:05:05.460
cover fast wherever you are. There's no time to look around or wait. Be like Bert. When

00:05:05.460 --> 00:05:11.740
there is a flash, duck and cover and do it fast. Here are some older boys showing what

00:05:11.740 --> 00:05:16.700
to do if the flash comes when you are not in the classroom. This is what to do if you

00:05:16.700 --> 00:05:22.930
should be in a corridor. You duck and cover tight against the wall this way. Remember

00:05:22.930 --> 00:05:28.520
to keep your face and the back of your neck covered tightly. Try to fall away from windows

00:05:28.520 --> 00:05:29.960
or doors with glass in them.

00:05:30.570 --> 00:05:33.970
Then, if the glass breaks and flies through the air, it won't cut you.

00:05:35.190 --> 00:05:37.350
You might be eating your lunch when the flash comes.

00:05:37.950 --> 00:05:39.670
Duck and cover under the table.

00:05:40.420 --> 00:05:44.750
Then, if the explosion makes anything in the room fall down, it can't fall on you.

00:05:46.270 --> 00:05:50.070
Getting ready means we will all have to be able to take care of ourselves.

00:05:50.960 --> 00:05:53.440
The bomb might explode when there are no grown-ups near.

00:05:54.420 --> 00:05:58.290
Paul and Patty know this, and they're always ready to take care of themselves.

00:05:59.530 --> 00:05:59.970
Here they are.

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:02.380
on their way to school on a beautiful spring day.

00:06:02.660 --> 00:06:04.720
But no matter where they go or what they do,

00:06:05.080 --> 00:06:07.360
they always try to remember what to do

00:06:07.360 --> 00:06:09.940
if the atom bomb explodes right then.

00:06:10.920 --> 00:06:12.480
It's a bomb. Duck and cover.

00:06:13.510 --> 00:06:15.250
Paul and Patty know what to do.

00:06:16.140 --> 00:06:18.600
Paul covered the back of his head so that he wouldn't be burned.

00:06:19.270 --> 00:06:21.670
And Patty covered herself with the coat she was carrying.

00:06:22.680 --> 00:06:24.660
They knew how to duck and cover.

00:06:24.970 --> 00:06:26.890
They acted right away when the flash came.

00:06:28.070 --> 00:06:29.970
If they had been at this doorway when the bomb...

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:35.980
flashed, Paul and Patty would have ducked and covered this way, like this girl. Heavy doorways

00:06:35.980 --> 00:06:42.780
are a good place to duck and cover. She will be safer, too. Here's Tony going to his Cub Scout

00:06:42.780 --> 00:06:49.350
meeting. Tony knows the bomb can explode any time of the year, day or night. He is ready for it. Duck

00:06:49.350 --> 00:06:57.230
and cover. Attaboy, Tony. That flash means act fast. Tony knows that it helps to get to any kind

00:06:57.230 --> 00:06:59.970
of cover. This wall was close by so

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:01.600
That's where he ducked and covered.

00:07:02.230 --> 00:07:03.330
Tony knew what to do.

00:07:03.980 --> 00:07:06.420
Notice how he keeps from moving or from getting up and running?

00:07:07.240 --> 00:07:10.260
He stays down until he is sure the danger is over.

00:07:11.540 --> 00:07:14.140
The man helping Tony is a civil defense worker.

00:07:14.710 --> 00:07:18.690
His job is to help protect us when there is danger of the atomic bomb.

00:07:19.410 --> 00:07:21.650
We must obey the civil defense worker.

00:07:23.040 --> 00:07:28.440
We must know how to duck and cover in the school bus or in any other bus or street car.

00:07:29.660 --> 00:07:29.860
Duck.

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:36.930
and cover. Don't wait. Duck away from the windows fast. The glass may break and fly through the air

00:07:36.930 --> 00:07:45.220
and cut you. Sundays, holidays, vacation time. We must be ready every day, all the time, to do the

00:07:45.220 --> 00:07:53.550
right thing. The atomic bomb explodes. Duck and cover. This family knows what to do, just as your

00:07:53.550 --> 00:07:59.670
own family should. They know that even a thin cloth helps protect them. Even a newspaper can save you

00:07:59.670 --> 00:07:59.890
I'm not.

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:04.520
But the most important thing of all is to duck and cover yourself,

00:08:04.990 --> 00:08:07.030
especially where your clothes do not cover you.

00:08:08.250 --> 00:08:10.910
No matter where we live, in the city or the country,

00:08:11.450 --> 00:08:14.530
we must be ready all the time for the atomic bomb.

00:08:15.600 --> 00:08:16.400
Duck and cover!

00:08:17.400 --> 00:08:18.680
That's the first thing to do.

00:08:18.930 --> 00:08:19.770
Duck and cover.

00:08:20.370 --> 00:08:25.530
The next important thing to do after that is to stay covered until the danger is over.

00:08:26.950 --> 00:08:29.170
Yes, we must all get ready now.

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:35.980
know how to save ourselves if the atomic bomb ever explodes near us. If you do not know just

00:08:35.980 --> 00:08:41.770
what to do, ask your teacher when this film is over. Discuss what you could do in different places

00:08:41.770 --> 00:08:47.790
if a bomb explodes. Older people will help us as they always do. There might not be any grown-ups

00:08:47.790 --> 00:08:54.790
around when the bomb explodes. Then you're on your own. Remember what to do, friends. Now tell

00:08:54.790 --> 00:08:58.330
me right out loud. What are you supposed to do when you see the flash?

00:09:02.930 --> 00:09:03.510
Thank you.
